    <briefdescription>
<para>What an evaluation of a material point changes, saved, and put back when this goes out of scope: the response and the tangents the material point keeps, and its state variables. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A particle describes its stiffness (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle_1aab0d22df342729365537585c8b3a6517" kindref="member">Particle::describeStiffness()</ref>) at a zero increment of its material point, which overwrites all three. It saves them first; they are put back also if the evaluation or the visitor throws, so the particle is left as it was found. The state variables are those the material point was assigned (MaterialPoint::getAssignedStateVars()). The density the material point keeps is not touched: it is taken once, at initializeYourself().</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MaterialPoint</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A material point with the public members <computeroutput>response</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>tangents</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
